cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SHAMS or this evaluation code, please cite the paper."
title: "SHAMS: An Audio-Grounded Pronunciation Benchmark for Levantine Arabic"
abstract: >-
  SHAMS pairs 1,300 Levantine Arabic utterances with four aligned tiers, audio,
  unvocalized orthography, diacritized Arabic and DIN-31635 phonetic
  transcription, stratified across five varieties and two source corpora, so
  that diacritization, grapheme-to-phoneme conversion, speech recognition and
  audio-to-phonetic transcription can be evaluated over the same material.
